# test/parity/SECTIONS -- runtime sections that exist only when a program asks
# for them, and the program that asks. All three compiling backends.
#
# WHAT THIS IS. Parts of each backend's runtime are emitted as literal text --
# WAT, C, LLVM IR -- rather than compiled from Mere, each gated behind a flag
# only a program using that feature sets. Text that is never emitted is never
# validated, never linked and never run, so a representation change walks past
# it and nothing goes red. That is not hypothetical; it happened three times in
# one day:
#
#   Q-068  mk_logger / mk_metrics: i32 locals against i64 signatures, a Logger
#          record with 4-byte fields where a field is 8, and on C a function
#          pointer typed `int` where the closure says `long long`. No compiled
#          program in the corpus used a capability.
#   Q-069  $mere_list_len: tag read as i32 at offset 0, payload at offset 4 --
#          the layout from before values widened. Nothing called it. LLVM's
#          list-len helper was broken twice over, separately.
#
# THE RULE THIS FILE ENCODES: a section with no program is untested code that
# looks like tested code.
#
# AND THE OTHER HALF: most sections audited this way were FINE. Four Wasm
# sections and one C section had no program; one of the five was broken. An
# untested section is a risk, not a defect, and a file that only recorded the
# defects would make the ratio unreadable.
#
# MODE is which invocation reaches the section, and it is load-bearing:
#
#   wasm       `mere -w`      | test/parity/ compiles all three of these ways,
#   c          `mere -c`      | so these sections are additionally required to
#   llvm       `mere -ll`     | be reached by SOME parity program. The named
#                             | program is a pointer, not a licence.
#   component  `mere -w --component`. Three sections exist only here and the
#              parity harness cannot reach them at all. scripts/
#              component_parity.sh builds and RUNS them against the
#              interpreter; this gate checks they are emitted.
#   none       genuinely unreachable, with the reason in the last column. There
#              are none today. The status is kept because the next one should
#              be a row with a reason rather than an absence, and because
#              section_coverage FAILS if a `none` row becomes reachable.
#
